  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two coils of self inductance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are connected in series combination having mutual inductance of the coils as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>. The equivalent self inductance of the combination will be</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/42385901-12f9-4eb9-80a7-9d42b05e90b4-image.png\" style=\"width: 220px; height: 69px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
